<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh Aug crude output up 6.3 pct at 1.996 mln T.</title>
<headline>Kazakh Aug crude output up 6.3 pct at 1.996 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's oil production, including gas condensate, rose 6.3 percent in August to 1.996 million tonnes from 1.878 million in July, the State Statistics Committee said.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for crude, natural gas and oil products output in its latest monthly statistical review:  </p>
<p> KAZAKH ENERGY OUTPUT	   Aug     July    Jan-Aug 96</p>
<p> Crude oil (million tonnes) 1.996    1.878	 14.69</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	  +6.3     +4.5	   n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	   +13.7     +5.7	 +11.4</p>
<p>Natural gas</p>
<p>  (million cubic metres)    521.6    459.8     4,095.5</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	 +13.4     +5.8	   n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	   +21.7     +2.8	  +7.3</p>
<p>  Gasoline (tonnes)	 226,500  192,000   1,617,000</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	 +18.0     +3.7	   n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	   +22.7    +30.7	 +19.5</p>
<p>  Diesel (tonnes)	   320,900  298,500   2,253,200</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	  +7.5     -3.0	   n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	    +3.2    +15.2	  +5.6</p>
<p>  Fuel oil (tonnes)	 287,600  291,000   2,399,100</p>
<p>   mth/mth pct change	  -1.2     +0.7	   n/a</p>
<p>   yr/yr pct change	    -1.3     +2.1	  +4.4</p>
<p>--Almaty newsroom +7 327 509410</p>
</text>
